INSERT INTO `consultant_register` VALUES
(1,3,'2025-01-10 16:59:00','2025-01-10','Pt seen in FGC,Complains of mild abdominal pain,\r\nbreast bilaterally active,uterus well involunted, minimal lochia loss with 2 pad change in 24 hours,no lower limb edema\r\nBaby seen in FGC,head and neck normal,good suckling,grasping and moro reflex.\r\nchest MWR,P/A No masses no organomegally,passed urine with 2 diaper change in 24 hours\r\nplan \r\n1.ct medz as per t sheet,\r\n2..encourage breastfeeding on demand\r\n3.monitor maternal and fetal vitals\r\n4.for possible discharge tomorrow',2,'2025-01-10 14:06:33'),
(2,3,'2025-01-11 09:35:00','2025-01-11','pt seen in fgc,no new complain today\r\nMother-doing well,breast bilaterally active,uterus well involunted,minimal lochia loss(3 pad change not fully soaked.\r\nBaby-doing well,head and neck normal,Good suckling and moro reflex,breast feeding adequately and retaining,chest MWR,passed urine and stool with 3 diaper change in the night and one in the morning',2,'2025-01-11 06:04:26'),
(4,4,'2025-01-10 06:50:00','2025-01-10','IV ATROPINE 1MG STAT\r\nIV NS ALTERNATE WITH D5% 2L IN 4 HOURS\r\nVITAMIN B COMPLEX IN 500 MLS OF N/S\r\nMONITOR VITALS\r\nIV ESOMEPRAZOLE 40MG STAT',2,'2025-01-11 06:41:10'),
(5,7,'2026-08-12 11:08:00','2026-08-12','Rhesus negative mother followed elsewhere admitted in advanced 1st stage of labour. progressed to SVD of a LFI of APGAR 8/1, 10/10. placenta and membranes complete EBL=500ls. developed small perineal tear(repaired succesfully). cord blood tested Blood group O positive.\r\nplan:\r\nMonitor for lochia loss.\r\nMonitor breastfeeding and milk let down before discharge.\r\nMonitor for lower limb edema.\r\nFor cord care.\r\nFor sitz birth[10-15 minutes twice a day ].\r\nconcider domperidone 10 mg if there is no milk letdown 24 hours post svd\r\nget Anti IGM for mother ASAP',7,'2026-08-12 08:08:45'),
(6,8,'2026-08-12 12:45:00','2026-08-12','Mother came in accompanied by the husband \r\n1.ADMIT\r\n2.MONITOR FOR PROGRESS OF LABOUR\r\n3.MONITOR MATERNAL AND FETAL VITALS',7,'2026-08-12 09:47:01'),
(7,8,'2026-08-12 15:05:00','2026-08-12','AT 2;00PM Called to review patient,on VE-4CM dilated,membranes still intact,percieves fetal movements,\r\nplan\r\n.Ct monitoring vitals,\r\n.minimise the number of VEs to avoid risks of infections',7,'2026-08-12 12:08:59'),
(8,8,'2026-08-12 16:10:00','2026-08-12','called to review patient,\r\no/e-patient doing welll,pain still bearable,no DOL reported,\r\nPLAN\r\n1] CT monitoring of labour\r\n2]Repeat V.E @ 6:00 PM\r\n3]CT monitoring maternal and fetal vitals.',7,'2026-08-12 14:11:57'),
(9,9,'2026-08-12 16:25:00','2026-08-12','patient came in as a referral from a peripheral facility with the compains of high BPs with no previous hx of hypertension,the high BPs were associated with right sided facial numbness with uncontrolled lacrimation for 1 day,with reports of drooling and deviation of the lips to the left,no other underlying medical condition reported,theres hx of contraceptive use{jadelle},\r\npara 1+0 last delivery 1.5 years ago\r\nO/E-Fully,conscious,no oedema/pallor/significant adenopathy,lichen planus-perioral,cns-mouth deviated to the left with obvious difficulty maintaining rt eye shut against significant  resistance,power g \r\nAt 16:30-Called to review patient,\r\nO/E-patient doing well,reports of improovement,still complaining of uncontrolled/involuntary tears from the right eye.\r\nPLAN\r\n1]Hourly monitoring of the BPs\r\n2]For U/A,CBC,UECs,PITC, Tomorrow.\r\n3]For possible Head CT scan to rule out possible CVA,/Bell\'s palsy',7,'2026-08-12 14:18:25'),
(10,7,'2026-08-12 07:20:00','2026-08-12','mother now para 2  doing day 1 post SVD,with an outcome of live female infant with a birth weight of 3.2 kgs and an apgar score of 8,9,10 \r\nToday NNC reported,\r\nMOTHER-doing well,breats not bilaterally active,uterus well involunted,minimal lochia loss,no lower limb edema,sustained grade 1 perineal tear-repaired,succesfully\r\n\r\nBABY-doing well,head and neck normal,good suckling and moro reflexes, chest MWR,\r\nON P/A-No masses,no organomegally,\r\nON GUT-passed urine and stool,\r\nNo abnormalities were noted,no extra digitalis.',7,'2026-08-12 14:33:26'),
(11,9,'2026-08-13 07:53:00','2026-08-13','patient still has bps at 100mmhg diastolic. no new complaints.\r\nplan: 1. do UECR/cbc\r\n1. needs CT Scan head ASAP',3,'2026-08-13 04:55:35'),
(12,8,'2026-08-13 07:59:00','2026-08-13','slow progress of labour noted with incoordinate weak uterine contractions. head at 3/5 up , cervical dilatation @6cm with regular featl @145b/min. has SRM 6hrs ago to clear liqour.\r\nplan:\r\n1. hoffmans solution to titrate against contractions\r\n2. close monitoring of fetal heart.\r\n3. mobilize',3,'2026-08-13 05:03:54'),
(13,7,'2026-08-13 08:04:00','2026-08-13','2nd day post delivery. lochia loss is normal. uterus involted well. baby f/feeding ok.\r\nsince mother is Rhesus negative and baby was tested Opositive, awaiting anti IGM before discharge. to also give BCG/OPV before  discharge',3,'2026-08-13 05:07:03'),
(14,9,'2026-08-13 10:30:00','2026-08-13','patient with hypertensive urgency,with a DDX of Bell\'s palsy secondary to hypertension,doing day 2 post admission with no new complains, today,bps still high at 146/108mmhg,but repoerts of improovement,\r\nO/E-in fgc,still involuntary lacrimation,lips still mildly deviated to the left side,\r\nG/E-No pallor/cyanosis/dehydration\r\nR.O.S-CVS-S2 MURMUR HEARD\r\nON P/A-No masses,no organomegally,no tenderness,no bruits\r\nplan\r\n1.For Head Ct scan urgent.\r\n2.For echo\r\n3.Awaiting UECs\r\n4.Adviced on physiotherapy[chewing gum]\r\n5.For artificial tears\r\n6.For facial muscle exercise.',7,'2026-08-14 08:58:37'),
(15,9,'2026-08-13 17:40:00','2026-08-13','@5;40pm\r\nIn consultation with dr muiruri;\r\nDX;CVA\r\nAccording to head ct scan done on 13/08/2026\r\n1]Features of left parietal border zone,acute ischemic infarct,left MCA territory infarct\r\n2]Two focal hypoattenuating areas within the left parietal subcortical region.\r\nno acute  intracranial haemorrhage,mass effect or hydrocephalus\r\nUECs-NORMAL,\r\nURINALYSIS-NORMAL\r\nCBCs-NORMAL\r\nPITC-NORMAL\r\nPLAN\r\n1]P.o Aspirin 150mg stat,\r\n2]P.o Amlodipine 5 mg OD\r\n3]For clopidogrel and atovastatin on discharge.\r\n4]For possible discharge tomorrow\r\n5]For family conference tomorrow to explain teh diagnosis of the patient',7,'2026-08-14 09:11:55'),
(16,9,'2026-08-14 10:16:00','2026-08-14','patient ding day 3 post admission DX;CVA according to head ct scan done on 13/08/2026\r\ntoday;nnc\r\n0/e-improoved\r\nall systems normal\r\nPLAN\r\nVISUAL ACUITY-6/6\r\nDISCHARGE HOME ON;\r\n1.P.O AMLODIPINE 5MG OD\r\n2.P.O ATOVASTATIN 20MG OD\r\n3.P.O ASPIRIN 75MG OD\r\n4.TOPICAL TEAR DROPS 2 DROPS TDS\r\n5.FOR LIPID PROFILE AS AN OUTPATIENT\r\n6.FOR ECHO AS AN OUT PATIENT\r\n7.FOR FOLLOW UP ON BPs DAILY',7,'2026-08-14 09:22:04'),
(17,7,'2026-08-13 20:31:00','2026-08-14','IGM vaccine administered to the mother@ 8;30PM\r\nPLAN\r\n1]For discharge tomorrow',7,'2026-08-14 09:35:36'),
(18,7,'2026-08-14 10:35:00','2026-08-14','Mother now para 2 doing day 3 post delivery,outcome of a live female infant with a birth weight of 3.2 kgs,lochia loss minimal,uterus well involunted,no lower limb edema,baby breast feeding well and retaining, passed urine and stool,no extra digitalis,no abnomalities noted,all systems normal\r\nPLAN\r\n1.FOR DISCHARGE TODAY\r\n2.TO GO HOME ON\r\n1]P.O AMOXICILLIN 500MG TDS FOR 5 DAYS\r\n2]P.O PCM 1 GM TDS FOR 3 DAYS\r\n3]FOR SITZ BIRTH 10-15 MINUTES TWICW A DAY FOR 2 WEEKS\r\n4]FOR CORD CARE\r\nTCA-MCH/FP IN 2 WEEKS',7,'2026-08-14 09:42:33'),
(19,8,'2026-08-13 15:00:00','2026-08-13','Patient with poor progression of 2nd stage of labour  due to cephalopelvic dispropotion with ,mild contractions doing day 2 post admission,head at 3/5,vervical dilatation @ 6cm with regular fetal heart rates @ 145b/min with SRM 8HOURS ago with clear liqour\r\nPLAN;\r\n1]FOR family conference in regarding diagnosis of patient and possible management\r\n 2]For FHG/PITC\r\n3]IV CEFTRIAXONE 2 GRAMS STAT\r\n@13;50\r\nPREPARE FOR EMERGENCY CS SECONDARY TO CEPHALOPELVIC DISPROPOTION\r\nPRELOAD WITH 1.5LITRES OF NORMAL SALINE ALTERNATE WITH DEXTROSE 10%.\r\n@14;20\r\nPatient succesfully deliverded a LIVE MALE INFANT,BIRTH WEIGHT @2.9KGS WITH AN APGAR OF 8/9/10,palcenta and membranes delivered,LVS stitched % hemostasis achieved,rectus stiched closed with subcuticular pattern,wound cleaned and dressed,VVT done,patient wheeeled out of theatre,\r\nEBL-500MLS\r\nPLAN\r\n1.CATHETER IN SITU,REMOVE ONCE PATIENT IS AMBULANT,\r\n2.FEED ONCE AMBULANT\r\n3.PAIN CONTROL-TRAMADOL 100MG PRN ON DAY ONE THEN \r\n DICLOFENAC PRN ON DAY 2 THEN PCM PRN DAY 3\r\n4.REMOVE DRESSING ON DAY 3 POST OP\r\n5.ENCOURAGE BREASTFEEDING & LATCHING & SUN BATHING',7,'2026-08-14 09:50:10'),
(20,8,'2026-08-14 10:07:00','2026-08-14','PATIENT DOING DAY 1 POST EMCS SECONDARY TO PROLONGED LABOUR/POOR PROGRESS WITH AN OUTCOME OF LMI @ 2.9KGS\r\nTODAY:Pain at the incision site \r\nO/E-in fgc,breast bilateraly active,lochia loss minimal,uterus well involunted, no lower limb edema,ambulating well,passsing urine well,feeding and retaining,\r\nBaby-doing well,head and neck normal,good suckling reflex,good moro reflex,good grasping reflex,chest MWR,p/a-no masses,no organomegally,passed stool,no hx of urine passed,no abnormalities noted,no extradigitalies,\r\nPLAN;\r\n1.PAIN MANAGEMENT AS PER T.SHEET.\r\n2.MONITOR  BREAST FEEDING AND LARCHING\r\n3.ENCOURAGE AMBULATION\r\n4.REMOVAL DRESSING ON DAY 3 POST OP\r\n5.FOR CORD CARE',7,'2026-08-14 10:21:33'),
(21,8,'2026-08-15 09:07:00','2026-08-15','patient now para 1 doing day 2 post EMCS secondary to poor progression of 2nd stage of labour with an outcome of LMI with a birth weight of 2.9kgs \r\nTODAY;NNC\r\n0/E-IN FGC,Breast bilaterally active,uterus well involunted,minimal lochia loss,no lower limb edema,ambulating well,feeding well and retaining,\r\nBABY-doing well,head and neck normal,breastfeeding well and retaining,chest MWR,no abdominal masses no organomegally,feeding well and retaining,passed stool and urine,testis well descended.\r\nPLAN;\r\n1]FOR DICHARGE TOMORROW\r\n2]FOR REMOVAL OF DRESSING TOMORROW\r\n3]FOR CORD CARE\r\n4]PAIN MANAGEMENT AS PER T.SHEET\r\n5]START ON P.O AMOXICLAV 625MG BD FOR 5/7\r\n6]MONITOR FEEDING BEFORE DISCHARGE',7,'2026-08-15 06:08:34'),
(22,8,'2026-08-16 10:07:00','2026-08-16','patient now para 1 doing day 3 post EMCS secondary to poor progress of 2nd stage of labour with an outcome of a LMI with a birth weigt of 2.9kgs\r\nO/E-IN FGC,Breast bilaterally active,uterus well involunted,minimal lochia loss,no lower limb edema ambulating well\r\nBABY-doing well,head and neck normal,breastfeeding well and retaining,chest MWR,passed urine and stool,testis well descended.\r\nPLAN\r\n1]FOR  DISCHARGE TODAY\r\n2]FOR REMOVAL OF DRESSING TODAY,\r\n3]FOR CORD CARE\r\n4]DICHARGE ON P.O AMOXICLAV 625 MG BD FOR 5 DAYS\r\n                               P.O PCM 1 GM TDS FOR 3 DAYS\r\n5]PATIENT EDUCATION DONE ON WOUND CARE AND CORD CARE\r\nTCA ON 24/08/2026',7,'2026-08-16 07:08:06'),
(23,10,'2026-08-18 13:36:00','2026-08-18','uterine evacuation done succesfully under sedation. allow home on;\r\n1. doxycyclline 100mg*2*5days\r\n2. pcm 1gm *bd*24hrs',3,'2026-08-18 10:39:07'),
(24,11,'2026-08-18 09:00:00','2026-08-18','patient who is a primigravid was on follow up at a peripheral facilty for anc clinics came in accompanied by the husband with complains of LAPS radiating to the back increasing in frequency and intensity,associated with LBP for more than 6 hours,no hx of pv bleeding was reported,no hx of DOL was reported.\r\nANC profile\r\nHB-14.5G/DL\r\nBG-A+\r\nURINALYSIS-NAD\r\nRBS-4.8MMOL/L\r\nPITC-NR\r\nVDRL-NR\r\nHEPATITIS B-NR\r\nO/E-IN FGC\r\nON P/A-FH-TERM,PRESENTATION-CEPHALIC,LIE-LONGITUDINAL,FHR-150B/MIN,\r\nON V.E-SHOW ON EXAMINING FINGER,CERVIX THIN,POSTERIOR,TIP OF FINGER\r\nPELVIS ADEQUATE\r\nPLAN\r\n1.ADMIT TO MATERNITY\r\n2.PATOGRAPH @4CM OF CERVICAL DILATATION',7,'2026-08-19 21:26:13'),
