(38,14,'2026-08-29 21:00:00','2026-08-29','patient who was brought in by relatives came in as a transfer in from a peripheral facility,with complains of confusion,oral thrush,dificulty in feeding,not being able to pass urine,with deviation of the lower lip,and aphaasic,patient is a known HTN patient on medication with history of hypertension and hypotension.had been on admission secondary to blood infection with no mproovement on discharge,a head ct scan was done on29/8/2026 with a conclusion of global cortical atrophy,an abdominal scan done on 26/08/2026showed hepatic steatosis grade 11,ovrely distended urinary bladder raising the possibility of urinary retention/bladder outlet obstruction,an ECG  done on 23/08/2026 showed atrial fibrillation with ashman phenomenon and controlled ventricular responce,A transthoracic echo done on 23/08/2026 showed hypertensive heart disease with borderline biventricular systolic functions,EF 50-55%TAPSE 1.6 CM\r\nMILD PULMONARY HYPERTENSION, previous hixtory of admission due to pneumonia,no history of previous  surgeries done,no history of blood transfusion.hx of bed sores grade 1 reported\r\npatient id a resident of gatundu with 7 siblings 1 deceased\r\nO/E-elderly,\r\nG/E-NO (pallor,cyanosis,bilateral pitting edema)\r\nVITALS-BP-100/64 PR-73,SPO2-92%\r\nR.O.S-RS-vesicular breath sounds,CVS-irregular heart rythm,CNS-GCS-13/15,ON MSS-UPPER LIMB-5/5,LOWER LIMBS-5/5,with bilateral pitting edema\r\nDX-NEWLY DIAGNOSED HYPERTENSIVE HEART DISEASE SECONDARY TO HYPERTENSION WITH LOWER LIMB EDEMA\r\nPLAN\r\n1)NYSTATIN ORAL DROPS 1 ML QID *5/7\r\n2P.O NIFEDIPINE  20 MG OD\r\n3)P.0 HARTEZE 10MG OD\r\n4)FOR PHYSIOTHERAPY\r\n5)ASSISTED FEEDING\r\n6)FOR PROPER BED SORES CARE\r\nSTOP ANTIHYPERTENSIVES\r\n7)REHYDRATE WITH DNS 500MLS STAT\r\n8)FOR 2 HOURLY BED TURNS\r\n9FOR CBC,UECs,U/A,PITC',7,'2026-08-31 09:22:06'),
