(107,'2026-08-18 12:14:00',11,9,'18/08/2026\r\n9:00 pm\r\nMother came as a walking [primigravida], accompanied by her mother and two [relatives]. Had no [complaints] of APs. On abdominal examination, fundal height 34/40, LROA, cephalic presentation and FHR 150 bpm. Vitals: BP 128/60 mmHg, P 80 bpm, temperature 36.6°C. On VE, cervix [soft], [show present], 1 cm dilated. Mother admitted due to early labour in primigravida.\r\n\r\n10:00 pm\r\nMother admitted to the labour ward with mild contractions. Advised to ambulate and not squat for good progress of labour.\r\n\r\n11:00 pm\r\nMother complained of pain occurring frequently, with back spray given and well tolerated.\r\n\r\n12:00 am\r\nVitals: BP 128/70 mmHg, P 80 bpm, temperature 36.8°C, FHR 143 bpm. Mother ambulating and doing squats. Mother still having mild contractions lasting for one minute.\r\n\r\n19/08/2026\r\n6:30 am\r\nBreakfast served, well taken and tolerated.\r\n\r\n8:00 am\r\nHandover done to mother and baby to day duty staff.\r\n\r\n8:45 am\r\nReceived mother in ward from night shift. Mother complained of lower abdominal pain radiating to the back. The contractions were strong.\r\n\r\n9:30 am\r\nDue plan: monitor every 2 hours, monitor maternal vital signs, P.I.C.E., reassure mother and encourage ambulation and squats. On VE, cervix located posteriorly, dilatation 5 cm, descent 3/5, effacement [unclear]. Contractions regular, lasting 1 minute.\r\n\r\n12:00 pm\r\nVitals: BP 131/52 mmHg, P 94 bpm, FHR [unclear]. Contractions strong and radiating to the back. Mother encouraged to ambulate.\r\n\r\n1:40 pm\r\nLunch served. Patient advised to eat and continue ambulating. Contractions regular and radiating to the back. Mother advised to ambulate.\r\n\r\n3:00 pm\r\nMother encouraged to ambulate. FHR regular at 150 bpm. Contractions every 4 minutes, lasting 1 minute and strong, radiating to the back.\r\n\r\n5:00 pm\r\nVital signs: BP 114/65 mmHg, P 104 bpm, FHR regular 140 bpm. On VE, cervix located posteriorly, dilatation 6 cm, descent 3/5. Mother encouraged to continue ambulation and squats.\r\n\r\n5:30 pm\r\nMembranes ruptured. Contractions increased in intensity and frequency. Mother encouraged to continue ambulating.\r\n\r\n6:00 pm\r\nMother handed over to N-shift staff for management and monitoring of mother and baby.\r\n\r\n6:10 pm\r\nReceived mother from day duty staff with moderate contractions.\r\n\r\n7:00 pm\r\nVitals: BP 117/70 mmHg, P 80 bpm, FHR 148 bpm. On vaginal examination, cervix was 6 cm dilated with severe abdominal contractions.\r\n\r\n9:00 pm\r\nMother progressing well with spaced contractions.\r\n\r\n10:40 pm\r\nMother progressing well with spaced contractions.\r\n\r\n11:00 pm\r\nOn vaginal examination, patient was still 6 cm dilated with severe abdominal contractions. Patient advised accordingly to promote progress of labour.\r\n\r\n11:30 pm\r\nMeeting held with family members and doctor. Mother advised to ambulate. Plan: monitor fetal and maternal vital signs.\r\n\r\n20/08/2026\r\n12:30 am\r\nPatient counselled regarding C-section. Consent obtained. Mother and family signed the consent.\r\n\r\n2:00 am\r\nPatient and family meeting conducted. Patient and relative signed consent.\r\n\r\n3:30 am\r\nMother prepared with N/S and [R/L]. Catheter inserted as per T-sheet.\r\n\r\n5:30 am\r\nMother called to theatre. Local anaesthesia administered. Vitals taken. Catheter inserted.\r\n\r\n6:05 am\r\nMother cleaned and draped. Abdomen incised in layers. FHR checked. Baby delivered at approximately 6:35 am. APGAR 9/10. Cord noted around the neck.\r\n\r\n6:40 am\r\nMother delivered placenta and baby. Baby [cried/was suctioned – unclear].\r\n\r\n6:50 am\r\nSwab count done. Wound cleaned and dressed. [Drain/other procedure – unclear]. Patient transferred to recovery.\r\n\r\n7:00 am\r\nPost-operative mother [stable/comfortable]. Encouraged to eat and breastfeed.\r\n\r\n8:00 am\r\nHandover done to mother and baby to day duty staff.\r\n\r\n8:30 am\r\nReceived mother and baby in ward post-operatively. Baby doing well with no complaints. Mother reassured. Mother complained of pain at incision site.\r\n\r\n9:30 am\r\nBaby doing well. Mother complained of pain.\r\n\r\n10:00 am\r\n[Medication] administered as prescribed by doctor.\r\n\r\n10:30 am\r\nBaby nasal congestion drops given, [number] drops in each nostril.\r\n\r\n11:30 am\r\nMother started on [medication/treatment]. One pad changed. Mother encouraged to breastfeed. Attachment and latching taught.\r\n\r\n1:00 pm\r\nMother and baby doing well. Mother encouraged to ambulate. Proper attachment and latching taught.\r\n\r\n2:00 pm\r\nBaby nasal congestion noted and unable to breastfeed. [Lochia/loss] present.\r\n\r\n2:40 pm\r\nMother\'s vital signs: BP 108/56 mmHg, P 111 bpm. Baby temperature 36.8°C.\r\n\r\n3:00 pm\r\nBaby received oral polio vaccine and BCG as documented.\r\n\r\n4:00 pm\r\nMother ambulating. Milk let-down is good. Lochia loss present but minimal. Baby breastfeeding well.\r\n\r\n5:00 pm\r\nMother and baby handed over to N-shift staff for management.\r\n\r\n6:10 pm\r\nReceived mother and baby in stable condition. Vitals: BP 118/68 mmHg, P 78 bpm.\r\n\r\n7:00 pm\r\nMother complained of pain. Medication administered as prescribed.\r\n\r\n8:00 pm\r\nMother taught about breastfeeding, proper attachment and latching.\r\n\r\n9:00 pm\r\nBaby crying due to hunger. Fed with [30 mL – ]. Medication administered as prescribed. Amoxyclav[625 mg –\r\n\r\n10:00 pm\r\nPatient settled and well tolerated. Vitals: BP 108/60 mmHg, P [unclear].\r\n\r\n21/08/2026\r\n6:00 am\r\nMother and baby had a calm night with no complaints.\r\n\r\n7:00 am\r\nBreakfast served, well taken and well tolerated.\r\n\r\n8:00 am\r\nHandover done of mother and baby to day duty staff. Vitals: BP 110/70 mmHg, P 75b/min. Baby temperature 36.0°C.\r\n\r\n10:00 am\r\nMother and baby doing well with no complaints.','MOTHER AND BABY OKAY','2026-08-18 12:14:00'),
