er prepared with N/S and [R/L]. Catheter inserted as per T-sheet.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n5:30 am\r\nMother called to theatre. Local anaesthesia administered. Vitals taken. Catheter inserted.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n6:05 am\r\nMother cleaned and draped. Abdomen incised in layers. FHR checked. Baby delivered at approximately 6:35 am. APGAR 9/10. Cord noted around the neck.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n6:40 am\r\nMother delivered placenta and baby. Baby [cried/was suctioned – unclear].\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n6:50 am\r\nSwab count done. Wound cleaned and dressed. [Drain/other procedure – unclear]. Patient transferred to recovery.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n7:00 am\r\nPost-operative mother [stable/comfortable]. Encouraged to eat and breastfeed.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n8:00 am\r\nHandover done to mother and baby to day duty staff.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n8:30 am\r\nReceived mother and baby in ward post-operatively. Baby doing well with no complaints. Mother reassured. Mother complained of pain at incision site.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n9:30 am\r\nBaby doing well. Mother complained of pain.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n10:00 am\r\n[Medication] administered as prescribed by doctor.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n10:30 am\r\nBaby nasal congestion drops given, [number] drops in each nostril.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n11:30 am\r\nMother started on [medication/treatment]. One pad changed. Mother encouraged to breastfeed. Attachment and latching taught.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n1:00 pm\r\nMother and baby doing well. Mother encouraged to ambulate. Proper attachment and latching taught.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n2:00 pm\r\nBaby nasal congestion noted and unable to breastfeed. [Lochia/loss] present.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n2:40 pm\r\nMother\'s vital signs: BP 108/56 mmHg, P 111 bpm. Baby temperature 36.8°C.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n3:00 pm\r\nBaby received oral polio vaccine and BCG as documented.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n4:00 pm\r\nMother ambulating. Milk let-down is good. Lochia loss present but minimal. Baby breastfeeding well.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n5:00 pm\r\nMother and baby handed over to N-shift staff for management.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n6:10 pm\r\nReceived mother and baby in stable condition. Vitals: BP 118/68 mmHg, P 78 bpm.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n7:00 pm\r\nMother complained of pain. Medication administered as prescribed.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n8:00 pm\r\nMother taught about breastfeeding, proper attachment and latching.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n9:00 pm\r\nBaby crying due to hunger. Fed with [30 mL – exact feed unclear]. Medication administered as prescribed. Amoxyl [625 mg – unclear].\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n10:00 pm\r\nPatient settled and well tolerated. Vitals: BP 108/60 mmHg, P [unclear].\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n21/08/2026\r\n6:00 am\r\nMother and baby had a calm night with no complaints.\r\nNurse: [Signature appears to read “Chris B.M.” – not fully clear]\r\n7:00 am\r\nBreakfast served, well taken and well tolerated.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n8:00 am\r\nHandover done of mother and baby to day duty staff. Vitals: BP 110/70 mmHg, P [unclear]. Baby temperature 36.0°C.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n10:00 am\r\nMother and baby doing well with no complaints.\r\nNurse: [Signature unclear]\r\n\r\nOn Thu, 25 Jun 2026, 13:46 Emily Wachira, <wachiraemily20> wrote:\r\n(3) Comment: MOTHER AND BABY OKAY','',NULL,3285,'2026-08-21 12:15:19','yes','2026-08-21 09:15:19'),
