(2280,'New IPD Nurse Note','ipd','Add New Nurse Note for IPD Number: (IPDN12) Patient: JOYCE KAMAU NJERI (3312) Case ID: 156 with consultant doctor  Teddy Hiribae (005). \r\n\r\nNurse Note Details:\r\n(1) Nurse Name: Nyambura (9)\r\n(2) Note: 7:20 AM: Admitted accompanied by husband with complaints of lower abdominal pains (LAPS) radiating to the back. On abdominal exam: fundal height 39/40 weeks, lie longitudinal, presentation cephalic, 3/5 engagement, fetal heart rate (FHR) 148 b/min. On vaginal exam (VE): show present, cervix 1 cm dilated. Vitals: BP 130/90 mmHg, Pulse 90 b/min.\r\n​7:40 AM: Admitted to ward; contractions increasing in intensity.\r\n​8:00 AM: Vitals: BP 130/80 mmHg, Pulse 80 b/min. FHR: 149 b/min with mild contractions.\r\n​4:00 AM: Membranes ruptured with clear liquor.\r\n​6:30 AM: Patient ambulating with moderate contractions. Vitals: BP 120/80 mmHg, Pulse 88 b/min, FHR 140 b/min.\r\n​7:00 AM: Breakfast served and well tolerated.\r\n​7:35 AM: VE shows cervix 6 cm dilated, descent 3/5 with a thick cervix. Labor progressing well with moderate contractions. Vitals: BP 128/80 mmHg, Pulse 80 b/min, FHR 149 b/min.\r\n​8:00 AM: Handed over to day duty staff in a fair condition.\r\n​8:30 AM: Received in ward with complaints of LAPS and strong contractions radiating to the back. Regular FHR at 134 b/min.\r\n​9:30 AM: VE: Show present, clear liquor, cervix 8 cm dilated, descent 2/5, caput +1.\r\n​10:00 AM: Reviewed by Dr. Antonio. VE: cervix fully dilated, descent 2/5, FHR regular at 144 b/min. Plan: monitor for 2 hours to determine progress.\r\n​11:05 AM: Strong contractions radiating to the back; mother doing squats to allow proper descent.\r\n​12:00 PM: Reviewed by Dr. Antonio. VE: cervix fully dilated, caput ++1. Decision made for Emergency C-Section (Em CS). Consent signed. IV line cannulated, CefTRIAXONE 2g administered, pre-loading started. Vitals: BP 125/75 mmHg, Pulse 86 b/min.\r\n​2:00 PM: Taken to theatre. Spinal anesthesia administered. Incision made; baby extracted with difficulty (APGAR: 7¹ 9⁵ 10¹⁰, birth weight: 4.95 kg). Placenta delivered complete; normal hemostasis achieved. Catheter inserted. Mother wheeled to ward for postnatal care. Vitamin K 1mg IM administered. 10?xtrose (10 D10) administered PO to baby (tolerated well). Baby\'s RBS: 2.3–3 mmol/L.\r\n​3:00 PM: Breastfeeding initiated (proper milk let-down, teaching on latching/attachment initiated).\r\n​5:00 PM: Mother taught on proper attachment. Pain at incision site noted. Vitals: BP 120/80 mmHg, Pulse 85 b/min.\r\n​6:00 PM: Handed over to night shift for monitoring and management. Vitals: BP 131/73 mmHg, Pulse 117 b/min.\r\n​6:10 PM: Received mother and baby from day duty in stable condition.\r\n​7:00 PM: Vitals: BP 130/70 mmHg, Pulse 80 b/min. Baby temp: 36.6 °C. Minimal lochia loss; baby breastfeeding well.\r\n​9:00 PM: Mother complained of pain; analgesia administered as prescribed on T-sheet. Mother ambulating.\r\n​10:00 PM: Mother took sips of water (retained). Baby breastfeeding well.\r\n​12:00 AM: Mother slept well; baby doing well. Vitals: BP 118/70 mmHg, Pulse 80 b/min. Baby temp: 36.5 °C, breathing well.\r\n​19/08/2026\r\n​5:00 AM: Mother and baby had a calm night with no complaints.\r\n​6:30 AM: Breakfast served and well tolerated.\r\n​8:00 AM: Handed over to day duty staff.\r\n​8:15 AM: Received in stable condition. Mild-to-moderate incision pain; lochia rubra minimal; pad changed 3 times since yesterday night. Milk let-down proper with good latching.\r\n​9:30 AM: Baby\'s RBS: 2.6 mmol/L. Nan 10 ml administered (tolerated well).\r\n​10:00 AM: Nan 10 ml administered (tolerated well).\r\n​12:00 PM: Vitals: BP 123/78 mmHg, Pulse 114 b/min. Baby temp: 35.9 °C.\r\n​1:40 PM: Lunch served and well tolerated. Pain at incision site treated with IM Diclofenac 75 mg.\r\n​2:00 PM: Ampiclox 0.6 ml PO administered to baby. Nasal congestion resolved; baby passed stool and urine.\r\n​4:00 PM: Mother and baby doing well. Breastfeeding well with good latching. Incision pain reduced; lochia minimal.\r\n​6:00 PM: Handed over to night shift staff.\r\n​6:10 PM: Received mother and baby in stable condition.\r\n​8:30 PM: Prescribed medications administered to mother and baby per T-sheet: Amoxiclav 625 mg BD (mother), Ampiclox 0.6 ml drops (baby).\r\n​9:00 PM: Supper served; mother walked and breastfed well.\r\n​9:40 PM: Vitals: BP 120/70 mmHg, Pulse 80 b/min. Baby temp: 36.6 °C.\r\n​11:30 PM: Baby\'s RBS: 3.4 mmol/L; advised on exclusive breastfeeding.\r\n​20/08/2026\r\n​6:00 AM: Mother and baby had a calm night. Handed over to day duty staff.\r\n​8:10 AM: Received mother and baby in stable condition. Breastfeeding well. Mild/reduced incision pain, minimal lochia. Mother encouraged to consider contraceptive methods prior to discharge.\r\n​12:00 PM: Medications administered: PO Amoxiclav 625 mg, Paracetamol 1g. Baby given PO Ampiclox drops (tolerated well).\r\n​1:00 PM: Lunch served and well tolerated. Baby breastfeeding well. Minimal pain at incision site; pad not fully soaked (minimal lochia). Baby\'s temp: 35.7 °C.\r\n​2:00 PM: Vitals: BP 104/55 mmHg, Pulse 104 b/min.\r\n​3:00 PM: Baby vaccinated: Oral Polio Vaccine (OPV) and Subcutaneous BCG given.\r\n​5:00 PM: Mother and baby doing well; breastfeeding properly, minimal lochia. Handed over to night shift in stable condition.\r\n​6:00 PM: Mother and baby handed over in stable condition.\r\n​6:10 PM: Received mother and baby. Vitals: BP 120/70 mmHg, Pulse 80 b/min. Baby temp: 36.6 °C.\r\n​6:50 PM: Medications administered per T-sheet: Amoxiclav 625 mg (mother), Ampiclox (baby).\r\n​8:00 PM: Dinner served and well tolerated.\r\n​9:00 PM: Mother and baby doing well; no complaints; baby breastfeeding well.\r\n​11:00 PM: Ampiclox drops administered to baby as prescribed.\r\n​2:00 AM: Mother and baby had a calm night with no complaints.\r\n​6:00 AM: Breakfast served and well tolerated.\r\n​7:00 AM: Handed over mother and baby to day duty staff.\r\n​8:00 AM: Vitals: BP 120/80 mmHg, Pulse 80 b/min.\r\n(3) Comment: Mother and baby doind well','',7,1,'2026-08-21 17:35:51','yes','2026-08-21 14:35:51'),
