(2630,'New IPD Nurse Note','ipd','Add New Nurse Note for IPD Number: (IPDN14) Patient: TERESIA KARANJA NJERI (3889) Case ID: 164 with consultant doctor  Teddy Hiribae (005). \r\n\r\nNurse Note Details:\r\n(1) Nurse Name: Nyambura (9)\r\n(2) Note: Patient came to hospital accompanied by relatives. Patient\'s relatives reported patient was discharged from High Care Medical Centre. On general examination, patient looked confused and dehydrated. Relative reported that the patient had been choking from morning. Vitals: BP 100/64 mmHg, P 73 bpm, SpO₂ 92%. Called the doctor for review. On auscultation, there was irregular heart rhythm.\r\n9:40 pm:\r\nPatient admitted to the ward for further treatment. Dr. Antony came to review. On examination, patient had a distended abdomen due to urine retention. Patient with coccygeal bedsores\r\n10:00 pm – Plan:\r\nCannulation\r\nCatheterization\r\nDraw samples for UECS\r\nRehabilitation\r\nAssisted feeding\r\nWard care with petroleum jelly, 2 hourly turning\r\nPhysiotherapy\r\nAntihypertensives to be held until BP is stable\r\nPatient on Hartaze 10 mg / Nifedipine 20 mg OD\r\nCT with nystatin with providine and D5\r\nECG provided and DS\r\n11:00 pm:\r\nCannulation done. Catheterization instituted. DS administered as prescribed.\r\n11:30 pm:\r\nPatient turned to the left side. Vitals: BP 100/64 mmHg, P 75 bpm, SpO₂ 90%.\r\n11:40 pm:\r\nBlood drawn for UECS. Urine specimen collected.\r\n2:00 am:\r\nPatient turned to the right side. Vitals: BP 114/64 mmHg, P 70 bpm, SpO₂ 92%. Patient is calm but still not talking.\r\n6:00 am:\r\nPatient had a calm night but is still not talking.\r\n7:00 am:\r\nPatient served breakfast; assisted feeding but refused.\r\n7:10 am:\r\nFBS done: 7.8 mmol/L. Patient still not talking. Nystatin administered.\r\n7:30 am:\r\nHanded over patient to day duty staff.\r\nDay Duty\r\n7:30 am:\r\nPatient received from night staff for continued management.\r\nVitals: BP 86/51 mmHg, HR 63 bpm, SpO₂ 96%. Patient is producing incomprehensible sounds, urine draining, output 1800 mL.\r\n9:20 am:\r\nPatient was assisted with bathing and lotion care done.\r\n10:00 pm:\r\nTried to feed patient porridge; patient refused. Also deficit in following. Informed the ward doctor and IV RL was ordered. Patient refused cannulation; Nystatin doctor was informed.\r\nVitals: BP 111/66 mmHg, HR 91 bpm.\r\n5:00 pm:\r\nPatient was cannulated. IV RL was administered as prescribed.\r\n5:30 pm:\r\nPatient handed over to night staff in a poor condition on IV RL drip.\r\n6:00 pm:\r\nReceived patient in a fairly stable condition. Vitals: BP 100/60 mmHg, P 90, SpO₂ 91%.\r\n7:00 pm:\r\nServed some food but refused to eat.\r\n8:00 pm:\r\nDue medication administered as prescribed.\r\n10:00 pm:\r\nVitals: BP 110/60 mmHg, P 70 bpm.\r\n2:00 am:\r\nPatient sleeping well, refused to be turned.\r\n6:00 am:\r\nPatient had a calm night but she is confused.\r\n7:00 am:\r\nAssisted the patient to take breakfast but only took 3 sips of tea and refused the rest.\r\n7:40 am:\r\nVitals: BP 115/59 mmHg, P 80 bpm, SpO₂ 84%.\r\n8:00 am:\r\nHanded over patient to morning duty staff.\r\n(3) Comment: patient handed over to day shift staff','',7,1,'2026-08-31 12:53:21','yes','2026-08-31 09:53:21'),
